  "Number": 3,
  "Question": "Which triplet of numbers has a sum NOT equal to \\(1?\\)",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\((\\frac12,\\frac13,\\frac16)\\)",
    "B": "\\((2,-2,1)\\)",
    "C": "\\((0.1,0.3,0.6)\\)",
    "D": "\\((1.1,-2.1,1.0)\\)",
    "E": "\\((-\\frac32,-\\frac52,5)\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "D",
  "Solution": "Compute each sum, keeping the negative signs and using a common denominator where needed:\n\\[\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\text{A: }&\\frac12+\\frac13+\\frac16=\\frac{3+2+1}{6}=1,\\\\\n\\text{B: }&2+(-2)+1=0+1=1,\\\\\n\\text{C: }&0.1+0.3+0.6=0.4+0.6=1,\\\\\n\\text{D: }&1.1+(-2.1)+1.0=-1+1=0,\\\\\n\\text{E: }&-\\frac32-\\frac52+5=-4+5=1.\n\\end{aligned}\n\\]\nOnly the triplet in \\(\\boxed{\\text{D}}\\) has a sum different from \\(1\\).",
